9:T112f,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What is AI Waitlist Rescue?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"AI Waitlist Rescue is Trayago's search feature for travellers whose direct train is waitlisted or fully booked. Instead of only checking the one train you had in mind, it evaluates alternative ways to cover the same route — including split journeys that break the trip into two or more legs through an intermediate station — and surfaces combinations where seats may still be available."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is a split train journey?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A split journey completes one route using two or more separate trains. Rather than a single Delhi–Patna service, you might travel Delhi–Kanpur on one train and Kanpur–Patna on another. Each leg is a separate booking with its own ticket, and the total journey time may be longer or shorter than the direct train."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Why would a split journey have seats when the direct train does not?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Long-distance trains are often booked end to end by passengers travelling the full route, so a popular city pair sells out first. Shorter segments of the same corridor, and less-searched trains serving intermediate junctions, can still have inventory. Splitting the journey lets you use whatever availability exists on each part of the route rather than needing one train to have space for the whole distance."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do I use AI Waitlist Rescue on Trayago?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Start a normal search from the Trayago home page: enter your origin station, destination station, and travel date. When direct trains are waitlisted or unavailable, use the AI search option on the results to look for alternative and split-journey combinations. Review the legs, timings, and availability shown for each option before deciding."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does Trayago guarantee a confirmed seat?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Trayago surfaces route options and the availability reported at the time you search. Railway inventory changes continuously, and confirmation is always determined by the official railway booking system. Treat the results as a shortlist of routes worth checking, not as a reserved seat."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do I need a separate ticket for each leg of a split journey?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Every train you travel on requires its own valid ticket for that segment. A ticket for the first leg does not cover the second. This also means each leg has its own class, quota, and confirmation status, and each can be waitlisted or confirmed independently."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What happens if the first train is delayed and I miss my connection?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"This is the main practical risk of a split journey. If the first leg arrives late, the second train will not wait, and the ticket for the missed leg is generally treated like any other unused ticket under railway rules. Leaving a comfortable buffer between legs, and checking live running status on the day of travel, reduces the exposure."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Are split journeys always cheaper or faster than a direct train?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Splitting a route can cost more in total than a single through ticket, and the combined journey time including the wait at the interchange can be longer. The reason to consider a split journey is availability — being able to travel at all on your chosen date — not price or speed."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I book the journey on Trayago?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Trayago is a journey planning and search platform; it does not issue railway tickets or process ticket payments. Once you have chosen a route, booking is completed on official platforms such as IRCTC."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is Trayago affiliated with IRCTC or Indian Railways?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Trayago is an independent travel intelligence platform and is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or operated by IRCTC or Indian Railways. References to IRCTC describe the official booking service where ticket purchases are completed."}}]}8:[["children",{"s":"__PAGE__","h":160,"d":{"r":["$","$2","c",{"children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"min-h-screen bg-[var(--bg-app)] px-4 py-8 sm:px-6 lg:px-8","children":[["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"BreadcrumbList\",\"itemListElement\":[{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":1,\"name\":\"Home\",\"item\":\"https://www.trayago.in\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":2,\"name\":\"AI Waitlist Rescue\",\"item\":\"https://www.trayago.in/ai-waitlist-rescue\"}]}"}}],["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"WebPage\",\"name\":\"AI Waitlist Rescue for Indian Train Travel\",\"description\":\"How Trayago searches split journeys and alternative route combinations across Indian Railways when a direct train is waitlisted or fully booked.\",\"url\":\"https://www.trayago.in/ai-waitlist-rescue\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-IN\",\"isPartOf\":{\"@type\":\"WebSite\",\"name\":\"Trayago\",\"url\":\"https://www.trayago.in\"}}"}}],["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$9"}}],"$La"]}],null,"$Lb"]}],"p":"$@c","v":null,"s":"$7"}}]]
