1a:["$","section",null,{"className":"mb-10","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-main mb-4","children":"What AI Waitlist Rescue does"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm sm:text-base text-main leading-relaxed mb-4","children":"A standard search answers a narrow question: which trains run directly between these two stations, and what is available on them? When the answer is \"all waitlisted\", the search is finished but your problem is not."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm sm:text-base text-main leading-relaxed mb-4","children":["AI Waitlist Rescue widens the question. It treats your origin and destination as endpoints on a network rather than as a single train pairing, and looks for viable ways through that network — including"," ",["$","strong",null,{"className":"text-main","children":"split journeys"}],", where the trip is broken into two or more legs that connect at an intermediate station. Each candidate route is checked for availability on every leg and for whether the connection actually works in practice."]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm sm:text-base text-main leading-relaxed","children":"The output is a comparison, not a single answer: the legs involved, the trains on each, the interchange station, timings, and the availability reported for each segment at the time of the search. You decide whether the trade-off is worth it."}]]}]
1b:["$","section",null,{"className":"mb-10","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-main mb-4","children":"Why splitting a journey can find seats"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm sm:text-base text-main leading-relaxed mb-4","children":"Availability on Indian Railways is not distributed evenly along a route. A long-distance train between two major cities is largely booked by passengers travelling the full distance, so the headline city pair sells out first and fastest. The same physical corridor, broken into shorter hops, often looks quite different."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm sm:text-base text-main leading-relaxed mb-4","children":"Three things create that gap. Shorter segments draw from a smaller, less contested pool of demand. Trains that terminate at or originate from an intermediate junction never appear in an origin-to-destination search at all, even though they cover part of your route. And regional or less-known services on the same stretch attract far fewer searches than the named express everyone tries first."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm sm:text-base text-main leading-relaxed","children":"Splitting the journey lets you use whatever availability exists on each part of the route, instead of requiring one train to have space for the entire distance on a date when it does not."}]]}]
1c:["$","section",null,{"className":"mb-10","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-main mb-4","children":"A worked example"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm sm:text-base text-main leading-relaxed mb-5","children":["Suppose you need to travel from"," ",["$","strong",null,{"className":"text-main","children":"Delhi to Patna"}]," on a fixed date and every direct option is deep in the waitlist."]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-5","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"bg-rose-500/5 dark:bg-rose-950/20 border border-rose-500/20 rounded-2xl p-5","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-sm font-bold text-main mb-2","children":"Direct search"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-xs sm:text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed","children":"Delhi → Patna. A handful of named expresses, all showing a long waitlist. Nothing left to try."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"bg-emerald-500/5 dark:bg-emerald-950/20 border border-emerald-500/20 rounded-2xl p-5","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-sm font-bold text-main mb-2","children":"Split journey"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-xs sm:text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed","children":"Delhi → Kanpur on one train, Kanpur → Patna on another. Two shorter segments, each drawing on its own pool of availability."}]]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm sm:text-base text-main leading-relaxed mb-4","children":"Kanpur is a natural interchange here: it sits on the route, is served by a large number of trains in both directions, and has enough frequency that a missed connection is inconvenient rather than journey-ending. Those properties matter as much as raw availability — a technically valid connection at a station with two trains a day is a worse option than a slightly slower one at a busy junction."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm sm:text-base text-main leading-relaxed","children":"The trade-off is real. You may pay more in total than a single through ticket, you will change trains, and the combined time including the wait at Kanpur may exceed the direct service. Against that: you travel on the date you needed. Whether that exchange is worth making depends on why you are travelling, which is why Trayago presents the options rather than picking for you."}]]}]
1d:["$","section",null,{"className":"mb-10","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-main mb-4","children":"How to use it"}],["$","ol",null,{"className":"space-y-3 mb-5","children":[["$","li","0",{"className":"flex items-start gap-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"shrink-0 w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-blue-500/10 text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 text-xs font-bold flex items-center justify-center mt-0.5","children":1}],["$","span",null,{"className":"text-sm sm:text-base text-main leading-relaxed","children":"Search normally from the Trayago home page — origin station, destination station, travel date."}]]}],["$","li","1",{"className":"flex items-start gap-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"shrink-0 w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-blue-500/10 text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 text-xs font-bold flex items-center justify-center mt-0.5","children":2}],["$","span",null,{"className":"text-sm sm:text-base text-main leading-relaxed","children":"Review the direct trains first. If something is confirmed or lightly waitlisted, take it; a split journey is the fallback, not the default."}]]}],["$","li","2",{"className":"flex items-start gap-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"shrink-0 w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-blue-500/10 text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 text-xs font-bold flex items-center justify-center mt-0.5","children":3}],["$","span",null,{"className":"text-sm sm:text-base text-main leading-relaxed","children":"Run the AI search for alternative and split-journey combinations when the direct options are not workable."}]]}],["$","li","3",{"className":"flex items-start gap-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"shrink-0 w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-blue-500/10 text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 text-xs font-bold flex items-center justify-center mt-0.5","children":4}],["$","span",null,{"className":"text-sm sm:text-base text-main leading-relaxed","children":"Compare the candidates on the things that matter to you: total time, number of changes, the buffer at the interchange, and availability on every leg."}]]}],["$","li","4",{"className":"flex items-start gap-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"shrink-0 w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-blue-500/10 text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 text-xs font-bold flex items-center justify-center mt-0.5","children":5}],["$","span",null,{"className":"text-sm sm:text-base text-main leading-relaxed","children":"Book each leg on an official platform such as IRCTC. Availability moves, so act on an option promptly once you have chosen it."}]]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm sm:text-base text-muted leading-relaxed","children":["One thing worth checking before you commit: the buffer between legs. A connection that looks fine on paper can be uncomfortable if the first train has a habit of running late."," ",["$","$L18",null,{"href":"/live","className":"text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 font-medium hover:underline","children":"Live train running status"}]," ","shows how the first leg is actually performing on the day."]}]]}]
1e:["$","section",null,{"className":"mb-10","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-main mb-4","children":"When a split journey is worth considering"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm sm:text-base text-main leading-relaxed mb-4","children":"It fits best when the date is fixed and travelling matters more than travelling comfortably — a family event, a start date, a return journey at the end of a holiday. It also helps on corridors where the direct service is a single premium train that books out months ahead, and during peak weeks when every direct option on your route is saturated at the same time."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm sm:text-base text-main leading-relaxed","children":"It is a poor fit when your dates are flexible — shifting travel by a day is usually simpler and cheaper than adding an interchange. It is also questionable if you are travelling with heavy luggage, small children, or elderly relatives, where changing trains at an unfamiliar station late at night carries a cost that does not show up in the timings."}]]}]
1f:["$","section",null,{"className":"mb-10","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-main mb-4","children":"Limitations you should understand first"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"bg-amber-500/10 dark:bg-amber-950/20 border border-amber-500/30 rounded-2xl p-5 sm:p-6","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-sm font-bold text-amber-800 dark:text-amber-300 mb-4 flex items-center gap-2","children":[["$","$L19",null,{"iconNode":[["circle",{"cx":"12","cy":"12","r":"10","key":"1mglay"}],["line",{"x1":"12","x2":"12","y1":"8","y2":"12","key":"1pkeuh"}],["line",{"x1":"12","x2":"12.01","y1":"16","y2":"16","key":"4dfq90"}]],"className":"lucide-circle-alert w-4 h-4 text-amber-600 dark:text-amber-400"}],"Before you book a split journey"]}],["$","ul",null,{"className":"space-y-3 text-xs sm:text-sm text-amber-900 dark:text-amber-200","children":[["$","li","0",{"className":"flex items-start gap-2","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-amber-500 mt-1.5 shrink-0"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"No guarantee of a confirmed seat. Trayago surfaces routes and the availability reported when you searched. Confirmation is decided by the official railway booking system, not by Trayago."}]]}],["$","li","1",{"className":"flex items-start gap-2","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-amber-500 mt-1.5 shrink-0"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Availability changes while you decide. Inventory moves continuously, and an option that looked open at search time can be gone by the time you reach the payment step."}]]}],["$","li","2",{"className":"flex items-start gap-2","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-amber-500 mt-1.5 shrink-0"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Every leg needs its own ticket. A ticket for the first train does not cover the second. Each leg has its own class, quota, and status, and any leg can itself end up waitlisted."}]]}],["$","li","3",{"className":"flex items-start gap-2","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-amber-500 mt-1.5 shrink-0"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"A missed connection is on you. If the first train runs late, the second will not wait, and the unused leg is treated like any other unused ticket under railway rules. Build in a buffer."}]]}],["$","li","4",{"className":"flex items-start gap-2","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-amber-500 mt-1.5 shrink-0"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Total time and cost can both be higher. Two tickets plus a wait at the interchange often adds up to more money and more hours than the direct train would have taken."}]]}],["$","li","5",{"className":"flex items-start gap-2","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-amber-500 mt-1.5 shrink-0"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Interchange conditions vary. Waiting several hours at a small station overnight is a different experience from waiting at a major junction with a retiring room and food."}]]}],["$","li","6",{"className":"flex items-start gap-2","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-amber-500 mt-1.5 shrink-0"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Booking happens elsewhere. Trayago does not issue tickets or take ticket payments; purchases are completed on official platforms such as IRCTC."}]]}]]}]]}]]}]
20:["$","section",null,{"className":"mb-10","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-main mb-5 flex items-center gap-2","children":[["$","$L19",null,{"iconNode":[["circle",{"cx":"12","cy":"12","r":"10","key":"1mglay"}],["path",{"d":"M9.09 9a3 3 0 0 1 5.83 1c0 2-3 3-3 3","key":"1u773s"}],["path",{"d":"M12 17h.01","key":"p32p05"}]],"className":"lucide-circle-question-mark w-6 h-6 text-blue-500 shrink-0"}],"AI Waitlist Rescue — frequently asked questions"]}],["$","dl",null,{"className":"space-y-5","children":[["$","div","What is AI Waitlist Rescue?",{"className":"bg-card border border-subtle rounded-2xl p-5","children":[["$","dt",null,{"className":"text-sm sm:text-base font-bold text-main mb-2","children":"What is AI Waitlist Rescue?"}],["$","dd",null,{"className":"text-xs sm:text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed","children":"AI Waitlist Rescue is Trayago's search feature for travellers whose direct train is waitlisted or fully booked. Instead of only checking the one train you had in mind, it evaluates alternative ways to cover the same route — including split journeys that break the trip into two or more legs through an intermediate station — and surfaces combinations where seats may still be available."}]]}],["$","div","What is a split train journey?",{"className":"bg-card border border-subtle rounded-2xl p-5","children":[["$","dt",null,{"className":"text-sm sm:text-base font-bold text-main mb-2","children":"What is a split train journey?"}],["$","dd",null,{"className":"text-xs sm:text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed","children":"A split journey completes one route using two or more separate trains. Rather than a single Delhi–Patna service, you might travel Delhi–Kanpur on one train and Kanpur–Patna on another. Each leg is a separate booking with its own ticket, and the total journey time may be longer or shorter than the direct train."}]]}],["$","div","Why would a split journey have seats when the direct train does not?",{"className":"bg-card border border-subtle rounded-2xl p-5","children":[["$","dt",null,{"className":"text-sm sm:text-base font-bold text-main mb-2","children":"Why would a split journey have seats when the direct train does not?"}],["$","dd",null,{"className":"text-xs sm:text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed","children":"Long-distance trains are often booked end to end by passengers travelling the full route, so a popular city pair sells out first. Shorter segments of the same corridor, and less-searched trains serving intermediate junctions, can still have inventory. Splitting the journey lets you use whatever availability exists on each part of the route rather than needing one train to have space for the whole distance."}]]}],["$","div","How do I use AI Waitlist Rescue on Trayago?",{"className":"bg-card border border-subtle rounded-2xl p-5","children":[["$","dt",null,{"className":"text-sm sm:text-base font-bold text-main mb-2","children":"How do I use AI Waitlist Rescue on Trayago?"}],["$","dd",null,{"className":"text-xs sm:text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed","children":"Start a normal search from the Trayago home page: enter your origin station, destination station, and travel date. When direct trains are waitlisted or unavailable, use the AI search option on the results to look for alternative and split-journey combinations. Review the legs, timings, and availability shown for each option before deciding."}]]}],["$","div","Does Trayago guarantee a confirmed seat?",{"className":"bg-card border border-subtle rounded-2xl p-5","children":[["$","dt",null,{"className":"text-sm sm:text-base font-bold text-main mb-2","children":"Does Trayago guarantee a confirmed seat?"}],"$L25"]}],"$L26","$L27","$L28","$L29","$L2a"]}]]}]
