25:["$","dd",null,{"className":"text-xs sm:text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed","children":"No. Trayago surfaces route options and the availability reported at the time you search. Railway inventory changes continuously, and confirmation is always determined by the official railway booking system. Treat the results as a shortlist of routes worth checking, not as a reserved seat."}]
26:["$","div","Do I need a separate ticket for each leg of a split journey?",{"className":"bg-card border border-subtle rounded-2xl p-5","children":[["$","dt",null,{"className":"text-sm sm:text-base font-bold text-main mb-2","children":"Do I need a separate ticket for each leg of a split journey?"}],["$","dd",null,{"className":"text-xs sm:text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed","children":"Yes. Every train you travel on requires its own valid ticket for that segment. A ticket for the first leg does not cover the second. This also means each leg has its own class, quota, and confirmation status, and each can be waitlisted or confirmed independently."}]]}]
27:["$","div","What happens if the first train is delayed and I miss my connection?",{"className":"bg-card border border-subtle rounded-2xl p-5","children":[["$","dt",null,{"className":"text-sm sm:text-base font-bold text-main mb-2","children":"What happens if the first train is delayed and I miss my connection?"}],["$","dd",null,{"className":"text-xs sm:text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed","children":"This is the main practical risk of a split journey. If the first leg arrives late, the second train will not wait, and the ticket for the missed leg is generally treated like any other unused ticket under railway rules. Leaving a comfortable buffer between legs, and checking live running status on the day of travel, reduces the exposure."}]]}]
28:["$","div","Are split journeys always cheaper or faster than a direct train?",{"className":"bg-card border border-subtle rounded-2xl p-5","children":[["$","dt",null,{"className":"text-sm sm:text-base font-bold text-main mb-2","children":"Are split journeys always cheaper or faster than a direct train?"}],["$","dd",null,{"className":"text-xs sm:text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed","children":"No. Splitting a route can cost more in total than a single through ticket, and the combined journey time including the wait at the interchange can be longer. The reason to consider a split journey is availability — being able to travel at all on your chosen date — not price or speed."}]]}]
29:["$","div","Can I book the journey on Trayago?",{"className":"bg-card border border-subtle rounded-2xl p-5","children":[["$","dt",null,{"className":"text-sm sm:text-base font-bold text-main mb-2","children":"Can I book the journey on Trayago?"}],["$","dd",null,{"className":"text-xs sm:text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed","children":"No. Trayago is a journey planning and search platform; it does not issue railway tickets or process ticket payments. Once you have chosen a route, booking is completed on official platforms such as IRCTC."}]]}]
2a:["$","div","Is Trayago affiliated with IRCTC or Indian Railways?",{"className":"bg-card border border-subtle rounded-2xl p-5","children":[["$","dt",null,{"className":"text-sm sm:text-base font-bold text-main mb-2","children":"Is Trayago affiliated with IRCTC or Indian Railways?"}],["$","dd",null,{"className":"text-xs sm:text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed","children":"No. Trayago is an independent travel intelligence platform and is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or operated by IRCTC or Indian Railways. References to IRCTC describe the official booking service where ticket purchases are completed."}]]}]
